.TH VIDEUR 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
videur \- Wayland proxy that controls which way a garnish VM's clipboard goes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B videur
.B \-\-display
.I socket
.B \-\-listen
.I socket
.B \-\-clipboard
.BR both | to\-host | from\-host | none
.RB [ \-\-protocols
.IR dir ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B videur
sits between crosvm and the host's Wayland compositor and passes on only the
clipboard data the policy allows.
.BR gerantd (1)
starts one for every VM with
.B Wayland=yes
and
.B Clipboard=
other than
.BR both ,
and gives crosvm its socket instead of the compositor's.
.PP
Copy and paste between the guest's own applications works in every mode,
even though sommelier passes the guest's clipboard through the host: videur
recognizes the guest's own offers and lets their pastes go straight back to
the guest. Drag and drop follows the same rules.
.PP
Only what the guest is given can be used: requests for objects it wasn't
given, binds to globals it wasn't offered, or anything that doesn't parse
end the connection. This holds even against a guest whose root user talks to
the GPU channel directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-display " socket"
The compositor's socket, such as
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wayland\-0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " socket"
Where to listen for clients (crosvm's
.BR \-\-wayland\-sock ).
An existing file there is removed.
.TP
.BI \-\-clipboard " policy"
.RS
.TP
.B both
The host pastes what the guest copies, and the guest what the host copies.
.TP
.B to\-host
Only the host pastes what the guest copies. The guest sees an empty
clipboard when a host application owns it.
.TP
.B from\-host
Only the guest pastes what the host copies. Host applications paste
nothing from the guest, though the host still sees that the guest copied
something, and its types.
.TP
.B none
Neither.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-protocols " dir"
Also read protocol descriptions from
.IR dir .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message.
.SH PROTOCOLS
To know which file descriptors go with which message and which objects a
message creates, videur reads the protocol descriptions in
.IR /usr/share/wayland ,
.I /usr/share/wayland\-protocols
and each
.B \-\-protocols
directory. Globals of other protocols are hidden from the guest, and
versions are capped at the ones in those files.
.PP
Always hidden:
.B ext_data_control_manager_v1
and
.BR zwlr_data_control_manager_v1 ,
which read the clipboard without focus, and
.BR gtk_primary_selection_device_manager .
The primary selection
.RB ( zwp_primary_selection_device_manager_v1 )
follows the same rules as the clipboard.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/garnish/vm/videur.log
Its output, when
.B gerantd
runs it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gerantd (1),
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5),
.BR garnish (7)
